#fs_team_data.csv — this is a template with fake sample data, not your real numbers. It shows you exactly the format the script expects columns: Driver, Session, LapNumber, LapTime, TyreAge, Notes.

#fs_analysis.py — reads that CSV and calculates:
Driver swap loss — finds any lap you've marked driver swap in the Notes column, compares it to normal pace that session, tells you how much time the swap cost
Lap time trend — per driver per session, fits a simple trend line across the run. Positive number = getting slower over the run (tire wear, fatigue), negative = getting faster (finding pace, fuel burning off)

